The Town Council shall meet for organization on the first Monday in January following the municipal election. The meeting shall be called in order by the town clerk and the oath of office shall be administered to the newly elected members as follows:

“L , do solemnly swear or affirm that:

I will well and truly perform the duties of Council Member (Mayor) of the Town of Sharpsburg, Georgia, to the best of my skill and ability, and as to me shall seem to me to be the best interest and welfare of said Town, without fear, favor or affection, so help me God;

I am not the holder of any unaccounted for public money due the state of Georgia or any political subdivision or authority thereof,

1 am not the holder of any office of trust under the government of the United States, any other State, or any foreign state which I am, by the laws of the State of Georgia, prohibited from holding;

I am otherwise qualified to hold office of Council Member (Mayor) of the Town of Sharpsburg according to the Constitution and laws of Georgia and the Town’s Charter;

I will support the Constitution of the United States and the Constitution of Georgia. Further, I do hereby attest that I am not now or never have been a member of any group or organization that would cause harm or be detrimental in any way, to this country, its government or its people.”

Following the induction ceremonies of the new members, the council by majority vote of all the members thereof, shall elect one of their members to be mayor pro tem. Said mayor pro tem shall serve for a four year term.

Oath of Office Ordinance Adopted: July 2, 2007
